  "change": "Share immutable statistics-residency checkpoints through Arc, detach on a new load, and avoid requeueing resident or already pending physical statistics. Keep first-load order, fallback and delayed publication.",
  "conclusion": "The checkpoint/restore path uses less sampled SQL CPU. This is NOT an accepted end-to-end throughput win: full read-only median TPS regresses at all tested client counts, while range results are mixed.",
  "source": {
    "go_revision": "23bff313186b8ceb61fcbe9faac43ae700e7fb14",
    "go_files_verified_equal_to_running_revision": [
      "pkg/statistics/table.go",
      "pkg/statistics/index.go",
      "pkg/planner/core/plan_cache.go",
      "pkg/planner/core/plan_cache_rebuild.go"
    ],
    "go_load_contract": "ColumnIsLoadNeeded and IndexIsLoadNeeded skip already fully loaded items; pending requests coalesce.",
    "remaining_plan_cache_gap": "Go lookupPlanCache -> adjustCachedPlan -> RebuildPlan4CachedPlan rebinds ranges without OptimizeAstNodeNoCache. Rust retains only access-path pins; bind_statement_markers replaces parameters with literals, and compiled Constant::eval rejects deferred/parameter constants. Reusable physical-plan and parameter-evaluation ownership are not implemented by this change."
  },
